  "conclusions": [
    "The input threshold and error check are inherited exactly, rather than introduced by the project.",
    "The original implementation reduces retrieval context by keeping resources in a Python workspace and returning thin retrieval acknowledgments; this is prevention rather than guaranteed oversized-result recovery.",
    "The pinned public code contains no automatic solution for oversized Python results or accumulated history; a large result still reaches the guard and fails.",
    "Our new multi-agent contexts and output contracts introduce additional failure pathways, so inheriting the guard does not absolve the project from managing its own payloads."
  ],
  "recommended_interpretation": "Retain the common 32k input constraint for the main comparison and improve payload/history management. Treat larger model context as a separate same-cap-for-all-systems ablation, rather than silently changing the inherited benchmark rule.",
  "privacy": "No secret configuration or credential files read. No code/pipeline/baseline changes, model calls, or paid evaluations."
